 "answer": "# Part A: Integers divisible by 3, 5, or 7, but not 17\n\n**Step 1: Count union of multiples of 3, 5, 7 (up to 5000)**\n\nUsing inclusion-exclusion:\n- |A|=\u230a5000/3\u230b=1666, |B|=\u230a5000/5\u230b=1000, |C|=\u230a5000/7\u230b=714\n- |A\u2229B|=\u230a5000/15\u230b=333, |A\u2229C|=\u230a5000/21\u230b=238, |B\u2229C|=\u230a5000/35\u230b=142\n- |A\u2229B\u2229C|=\u230a5000/105\u230b=47\n\nUnion = 1666+1000+714\u2212333\u2212238\u2212142+47 = **2714**\n\n**Step 2: Count those in the union that ARE divisible by 17** (to remove them)\n\nUsing inclusion-exclusion on 51, 85, 119 (i.e., 3\u00b717, 5\u00b717, 7\u00b717):\n- \u230a5000/51\u230b=98, \u230a5000/85\u230b=58, \u230a5000/119\u230b=42\n- \u230a5000/255\u230b=19, \u230a5000/357\u230b=14, \u230a5000/595\u230b=8\n- \u230a5000/1785\u230b=2\n\nUnion = 98+58+42\u221219\u221214\u22128+2 = **159**\n\n**Result:** 2714 \u2212 159 = **2555**\n\n# Part B: 85^542 mod 211\n\n211 is prime, so by Fermat: 85^210 \u2261 1 (mod 211).\n542 mod 210 = 122, so need 85^122 mod 211.\n\nSuccessive squaring:\n- 85\u00b2 \u2261 51, 85\u2074 \u2261 69, 85\u2078 \u2261 119, 85\u00b9\u2076 \u2261 24, 85\u00b3\u00b2 \u2261 154, 85\u2076\u2074 \u2261 84 (mod 211)\n\n122 = 64+32+16+8+2, so:\n85^122 \u2261 84\u00b7154\u00b724\u00b7119\u00b751 (mod 211)\n\nStep-by-step:\n- 84\u00b7154 = 12936 \u2261 65\n- 65\u00b724 = 1560 \u2261 83\n- 83\u00b7119 = 9877 \u2261 171\n- 171\u00b751 = 8721 \u2261 70\n\n**Result: 70**\n\n# Part C: Original Price\n\nCombined multiplier:\n1.25 \u00d7 1.25 \u00d7 0.85 \u00d7 0.90 \u00d7 1.20 = 459/320 = 1.434375\n\nP = 97.50 \u00f7 1.434375 = 97.50 \u00d7 320/459 = 31200/459 = 10400/153\n\n10400/153 = 67.973856\u2026\n\n**Result: $67.97**\n\n# Part D: CRT System\n\nx \u2261 7 (mod 13), x \u2261 1 (mod 7), x \u2261 18 (mod 19)\n\n**Combine first two:** x = 13k+7, need 13k+7\u22611 (mod7) \u2192 6k\u22611 (mod7) \u2192 k\u22616 (mod7)\nSo x = 91m + 85 (mod 91)\n\n**Combine with third:** 91m+85 \u2261 18 (mod19)\n91\u226115, 85\u22619 (mod19): 15m+9\u226118 \u2192 15m\u22619 (mod19)\nInverse of 15 mod19 is 14 (since 15\u00b714=210\u22611)\nm \u2261 14\u00b79 = 126 \u2261 12 (mod19)\n\nSo m = 19n+12, giving:\nx = 91(19n+12)+85 = 1729n + 1177\n\nSmallest positive: **x = 1177**\n\nCheck: 1177=13\u00b790+7 \u2713; 1177=7\u00b7168+1 \u2713; 1177=19\u00b761+18 \u2713\n\nFINAL: 2555; 70; 67.97; 1177"
